# The EverBetter tool catalog.
#
# One entry per tool a design may name. An entry is a DECISION, not an inventory
# row: the rationale is the part that stops the research being redone.
#
# Entries are read by the design validator, by preflight, and by the interview —
# which uses them to ask "use this, or is your process different?" instead of
# asking a person to do research.

@catalog
owner: Buzz, process owner
reviewed: 2026-10-06
source_of_truth: maxwell-k8s/charts for existence; this file for policy

# WHERE PHI MAY GO.
#
# This is the one policy every design inherits and none may widen. It is here,
# and not in the validator, because it is a business agreement — it changes when
# a contract changes, and a contract change should be a reviewable diff with a
# date on it rather than an edit to a rule.
#
# Buzz, process owner, stated on 2026-10-06 that EverBetter holds a BAA with both
# model providers. A model call is therefore inside the covered boundary, and a
# PHI source may reach a model step.
#
# ASSUMPTION, flagged because nothing here verifies it: the agreement references
# and their effective dates are not recorded below. "We have a BAA" was taken on
# the word of the process owner. Fill in baa_anthropic and baa_google with the
# agreement identifiers before this catalog is used for a process that runs on a
# real patient.
phi_may_reach_models: yes
phi_model_basis: BAA with Anthropic and with Google, stated by Buzz, process owner
phi_model_attested: 2026-10-06
phi_model_review_by: 2027-10-06
baa_anthropic: UNRECORDED — agreement identifier and effective date not supplied
baa_google: UNRECORDED — agreement identifier and effective date not supplied

@tool eb-appointment-service
provides: appointment_id, patient_ref, clinician, starts_at, duration_minutes, status
via: tools/eb-appointment-service
data_class: phi
may_not: leave the covered boundary
chosen: 2026-09, over polling FHIR directly
because: already deployed, and carries clinician and status in one call
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-09

@tool eb-form-builder-service
provides: submission_id, patient_ref, form, submitted_at, flagged
via: tools/eb-form-builder-service
data_class: phi
may_not: leave the covered boundary
chosen: 2026-09, over a bespoke intake form
because: clinicians already author forms in it; submissions carry a flag the triage rule needs
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-09

@tool keychain
provides: secret
via: security
data_class: credential
may_not: be written to a file or passed as a command-line argument
chosen: 2026-10, over a dotenv file
because: survives a reboot, is not readable by a stray process listing, and is macOS native
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-10

@tool local-ledger
provides: append-only rows
via: sqlite3
data_class: operational
may_not: hold PHI in clear text
chosen: 2026-10
because: no server, durable, queryable by anything
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-10

@tool eb-medication-service
provides: patient_ref, drug_name, rxnorm, dose, unit, frequency, status, recorded_at
via: tools/eb-medication-service
data_class: phi
may_not: leave the covered boundary
chosen: 2026-10, over reading the FHIR MedicationStatement endpoint directly
because: carries rxnorm beside the free-text name, which is what makes two spellings of one drug comparable without a model
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-10

@tool eb-intake-medications
provides: submission_id, patient_ref, reported_name, reported_dose, reported_unit, reported_frequency, free_text
via: tools/eb-intake-medications
data_class: phi
may_not: leave the covered boundary
chosen: 2026-10, over extending eb-form-builder-service to return submission bodies
because: the form service knows a submission exists and who made it, not what is inside one; a catalog entry claiming otherwise would assert a capability the service does not have
decided_by: Buzz, process owner
review_by: 2027-10
